🐛 Bug
The following short program does not compile.
#include "torch/torch.h"

int main() {
    torch::Tensor tensor = torch::ones({2, 2});
    tensor.fill_(0); // OK
    tensor = 0; // Gives compile error
}

Expected behavior
I would expect both the expressions 'tensor.fill_(0)' and 'tensor = 0' to compile and that they would yield the same result.
Looking at the source code 'aten/src/ATen/TensorOperators.h' the selected assignment operator is defined as follows:
inline Tensor & Tensor::operator=(Scalar v) && {
    return fill_(v);
}

That is, it is only defined for rvalues on the lhs of the assignment. I do not understand the rationale behind this restriction.
